---
import Compare from "../components/Compare.astro";
---

<section id="modules">
  <h2>22. Namespaces &amp; modules</h2>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>// Geometry/Point.cs
namespace Geometry;
public class Point(int x, int y)
&#123; public int X =&gt; x; public int Y =&gt; y; &#125;

// usage — namespace, not file path
using Geometry;
var p = new Point(1, 2);

// internal visibility stays in-assembly
internal class Helper &#123; &#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>// geometry/point.ts
export class Point &#123;
  constructor(readonly x: number, readonly y: number) &#123;&#125;
&#125;
// geometry/index.ts — barrel
export * from "./point.js";

// usage — file path, not namespace
import &#123; Point &#125; from "./geometry/point.js";

// module-private: just don't export
class Helper &#123;&#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <ul>
    <li>C# organizes by namespace + assembly. TS organizes by file + explicit <code>import/export</code>.</li>
    <li>TS needs <code>.js</code> in relative ESM imports under <code>NodeNext</code>. C# <code>using</code> never mentions files.</li>
    <li>TS <code>namespace</code> exists but is legacy — use ES modules + barrels.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<hr />

<section id="visibility">
  <h2>23. Access modifiers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Intent</th><th>C#</th><th>TypeScript</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Public</td><td><code>public</code> (top-level default is <code>internal</code>)</td><td><code>public</code> (default) / <code>export</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Private to class</td><td><code>private</code> (enforced)</td><td><code>private</code> (compile-time) or <code>#field</code> (runtime)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Subclasses</td><td><code>protected</code></td><td><code>protected</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Same project only</td><td><code>internal</code> / <code>InternalsVisibleTo</code></td><td>No equivalent — module privacy via non-exported symbols</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Static</td><td><code>static</code> + static ctors</td><td><code>static</code> + static blocks</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>public class Account
&#123;
  private decimal _balance;
  protected string Owner &#123; get; &#125; = "";
  internal string AuditId &#123; get; &#125; = "";
  private protected string Audit2 &#123; get; &#125; = "";
  public static string Bank =&gt; "Acme";
&#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>export class Account &#123;
  #balance = 0; // truly private at runtime
  protected owner = "";
  static bank = "Acme";
&#125;
// internal ≈ don't export from barrel:
const auditId = ""; // module-private
export &#123; /* only what callers need */ &#125;;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
</section>

<hr />

<section id="delegates">
  <h2>24. Delegates, lambdas, events</h2>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>public delegate int Compare(string a, string b);
Func&lt;int, int, int&gt; add = (a, b) =&gt; a + b;
Action&lt;string&gt; log = Console.WriteLine;
Predicate&lt;string&gt; isLong = s =&gt; s.Length &gt; 3;

public event EventHandler&lt;string&gt;? Renamed;
Renamed?.Invoke(this, "new-name");
// subscribe: obj.Renamed += Handler; //-= to remove</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>type Compare = (a: string, b: string) =&gt; number;
const add: (a: number, b: number) =&gt; number = (a, b) =&gt; a + b;
const log: (msg: string) =&gt; void = console.log;
const isLong = (s: string): boolean =&gt; s.length &gt; 3;

// events: EventTarget / EventEmitter, no keyword
import &#123; EventEmitter &#125; from "node:events";
const bus = new EventEmitter();
bus.on("renamed", (name: string) =&gt; console.log(name));
bus.emit("renamed", "new-name");

// DOM:
target.addEventListener("click", (e) =&gt; console.log(e));</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <ul>
    <li><code>Func&lt;A,R&gt;</code> ≈ <code>(a: A) =&gt; R</code>, <code>Action&lt;T&gt;</code> ≈ <code>(t: T) =&gt; void</code>.</li>
    <li>C# events are language-level with <code>+=/-=</code>. TS uses <code>addEventListener</code> / <code>EventEmitter.on</code> + <code>removeListener</code>.</li>
    <li>Multicast: C# delegates combine (<code>+</code>); TS typically holds an array of callbacks.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<hr />

<section id="overloads">
  <h2>25. Overloads, optional &amp; params</h2>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>string Format(int n) =&gt; n.ToString();
string Format(double n, int digits = 2) =&gt; n.ToString($"F&#123;digits&#125;");

int Sum(params int[] nums) =&gt; nums.Sum();
Sum(1, 2, 3);
Sum(new[] &#123; 1, 2 &#125;);</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>function format(n: number): string;
function format(n: number, digits: number): string;
function format(n: number, digits = 0): string &#123;
  return n.toFixed(digits);
&#125;

function sum(...nums: number[]): number &#123;
  return nums.reduce((a, b) =&gt; a + b, 0);
&#125;
sum(1, 2, 3); sum(...[1, 2]);</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <ul>
    <li>C# resolves overloads by arity/types at compile time. TS overloads are compile-time only — one runtime implementation handles all.</li>
    <li><code>params int[]</code> ≈ <code>...nums: number[]</code>. Spread <code>...</code> works at call sites and in literals in TS.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
